    "evidence": "MvidPreFrame lines244-273 reads two controller bytes per frame until fread reaches EOF; vidFrameCount is not a playback bound. Writer updates count separately. Exact cached bytes identified below."
  },
  {
    "url": "https://github.com/TASEmulators/fceux/blob/ce042d758a08f9434a6625580b2cc72495e8aa9a/src/oldmovie.cpp",
    "sha256": "f040f19c2d11bbed416afc26066200426c4eee51ffce017681d7587d64b2d2f0",
    "evidence": "movie_readchar/_addjoy lines469-542 and convert_fcm lines580-650 define declared controller byte length, wait-before-toggle events, and legacy zero-delta extension."
  },
  {
    "url": "https://github.com/TASEmulators/snes9x-rr/blob/450b6cba06996046f31ccc08561b258af75f4e35/movie.cpp",
    "sha256": "0345d2812adf48872297cdeedd8361237fa09d7448352011e071f8ff0d134dab",
    "evidence": "flush_movie writes BytesPerFrame*(MaxFrame+1); S9xMovieOpen reads that many bytes and then baseline controller state. This establishes one sample beyond the header frame count."
  },
  {
    "url": "https://github.com/emillon/zsnes/blob/master/src/zmovie.c",
    "sha256": "6f8ccebc6efd1865cf77d60c9aa94f765e637cb62a153e310e982c9d4f7199ce",
    "evidence": "zmv_record increments header.frames for each input sample; zmv_record_finish flushes input and writes a separate two-byte external chapter count. zmv_replay handles reset/chapter records without incrementing controller-frame count. Exact cached bytes identified below."
  },
  {
    "url": "https://github.com/TASEmulators/mednafen-rr/blob/master/src/movie.cpp",
    "sha256": "804d2c8fb02848602bc3141553142f3e5292c44b9a71bc23ebc6c610e4428149",
    "evidence": "Historical commented MDFNMOV_AddJoy block lines2006-2055 preserves the MCM serializer: command once per frame, port bytes on each call, playback stops on incomplete port read. Current MC2 code is separate."
  },
  {
    "url": "https://github.com/TASEmulators/mednafen-rr/blob/master/src/pce/input.cpp",
    "sha256": "abb7250820d6974c54c37737cc1c8716e11112da8ea6e33faa56625e7399d694",
    "evidence": "PCE device descriptors define two bytes per controller port. MCM PCE contains five ports after the command byte."
